TEXT 96 48 Left 3 ;#186 RC servo control from an adjustable DC voltage
TEXT 96 112 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iaGZOO33Z-o
TEXT 96 160 Left 2 ;A 0 to 5 V control voltage is sliced against a sawtooth to set the pulse width an RC servo reads as position.
TEXT 640 368 Left 2 ;Sawtooth generator: hysteresis comparator U1 and integrator U2
TEXT 96 940 Left 2 ;Control signal conditioning U3, and the output comparator U4
TEXT 96 1480 Left 2 !.step param VCTRL list 0 2.5 5
TEXT 96 1520 Left 2 !.tran 0 150m 50m 5u
TEXT 96 1560 Left 2 !.meas tran RAMP_PP PP V(RAMP) FROM 100m TO 150m
TEXT 700 1480 Left 2 !.meas tran PERIOD TRIG V(SERVO_PWM) VAL=2.5 RISE=3 TARG V(SERVO_PWM) VAL=2.5 RISE=4
TEXT 96 1600 Left 2 !.meas tran COND_LEVEL AVG V(CONDITIONED) FROM 100m TO 150m
TEXT 700 1520 Left 2 !.meas tran HIGH_TIME TRIG V(SERVO_PWM) VAL=2.5 RISE=3 TARG V(SERVO_PWM) VAL=2.5 FALL=3
